  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>On plotting the diagram of given value we get,</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/ee66ca0f-cfee-4dc7-871b-f137fbaad343-image.png\" style=\"width: 310px; height: 230px;\" /></p><p>Now given parabola is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Let a point on parabola be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Equation of tangent at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8757;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>R</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> lies on this tangent&nbsp;</p><p>Then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>i.e.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>.</p><p>So&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now triangle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;is right angled at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>, so&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is the orthocentre of the triangle.</p></blockquote>",
